<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalomo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalomo is a town in Southern Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, on the railway between Livingstone and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusaka">Lusaka</a>. It was the first administrative capital of North-Western Rhodesia under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a>, from about 1899 until the seat moved to Livingstone in 1907. Nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> settlement mounds gave their name to the Kalomo culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalomo.jpg" alt="Kalomo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LittleT889 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalomo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
